From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: XuanTie Linux SDK CI <noreply@linux.alibaba.com>
Date: Sat, 2 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] pyo3: gate PyUnicode_READY call at compile time for Python
 3.13

PyUnicode_READY() has been a no-op since CPython 3.12 and was removed in
3.13. In pyo3 0.15.2 the function *definition* in
ffi/cpython/unicodeobject.rs is correctly gated with
#[cfg(not(Py_3_12))], but the call site in types/string.rs uses a
*runtime* `if cfg!(not(Py_3_12))`, so the reference is still compiled for
Python 3.12+ and building against python3 3.13 fails with:

    error[E0425]: cannot find function, tuple struct or tuple variant
    `PyUnicode_READY` in module `ffi`

Switch the call site to a compile-time #[cfg(not(Py_3_12))] block so the
reference is dropped for Python 3.12+, matching the gating of the
definition. Behaviour is unchanged for Python <= 3.11.

This patch is applied to the vendored pyo3 0.15.2 crate
(patchdir=${CARGO_HOME}/bitbake/pyo3-0.15.2), not to the cryptography
sources.

Upstream-Status: Backport [https://github.com/PyO3/pyo3 commit 0.16 series]
---
 src/types/string.rs | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/types/string.rs b/src/types/string.rs
--- a/src/types/string.rs
+++ b/src/types/string.rs
@@ -227,7 +227,8 @@ impl PyString {
     pub unsafe fn data(&self) -> PyResult<PyStringData<'_>> {
         let ptr = self.as_ptr();

-        if cfg!(not(Py_3_12)) {
+        #[cfg(not(Py_3_12))]
+        {
             #[allow(deprecated)]
             let ready = ffi::PyUnicode_READY(ptr);
             if ready != 0 {
